    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Kkov6bcyvPJhYXpEnDKKEp)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`, which already contains #447 (`sp-vulpea-ui-view`, merged 2026-11-13); this PR edits that module.\n- Independent of every other open PR (none touches `sp-vulpea.org` or `sp-vulpea-ui-view.el`).\n- If merged out of order: nothing breaks.\n- After merging: restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`); nothing to retarget.\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Request:** long lines in each widget section of the `vulpea-ui-view` (`M-o v`) are cut at the window edge; wrap them so the whole content is readable.\n- **New options** (group `sp-vulpea-ui-view`):\n  - `sp-vulpea-ui-view-wrap-lines` (default `t`): wrap at word boundaries in the view buffer only (`visual-line-mode`, `truncate-lines` nil). Nil gives the old look.\n  - `sp-vulpea-ui-view-wrap-indent` (default `t`): indent the wrapped part like the line start (`visual-wrap-prefix-mode`, Emacs 30+; older Emacs wraps without the indent).\n- **Where it applies:** in the mode body, after the first mount, and after a `g` refresh (so a changed option takes effect on refresh). The sidebar and other buffers are not touched.\n- Docs: new bullet-point part \"Line wrapping\" and \"Wrapping the lines\" in `sp-vulpea.org`; `.el` and tests re-tangled.\n- Tests: 3 new ERT tests (13 in total pass on Emacs 29.3 batch). `when-let*` only, no CHANGELOG edit.\n- **Untested by Claude:** real `vulpea-ui`/`vui` and the GUI (stubbed in tests). Not known whether `vui` sets its own `line-prefix`/`wrap-prefix` on widget text, or resets `truncate-lines` after mount; if wrapping does not show, tell me.\n\n## Manual testing\n\nMac, `~/.config/emacs-modular`, a note with backlinks that have long lines.\n\n- [ ] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 456-vulpea-ui-view-wrap-lines; git checkout 456-vulpea-ui-view-wrap-lines`, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -l tests/sp-vulpea-ui-view-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → 13 pass\n- [ ] `M-o v` (untested by Claude): long backlink and other widget lines wrap at the window edge, no horizontal cut-off\n- [ ] Narrow the view frame: lines re-wrap to the new width\n- [ ] Emacs 30+: a wrapped line is indented like its start (check `M-: emacs-version`); older Emacs: wraps without indent\n- [ ] `TAB` widget toggling, `g` refresh, click a backlink still work\n- [ ] `(setq sp-vulpea-ui-view-wrap-indent nil)`, `g`: wraps without indent\n- [ ] `(setq sp-vulpea-ui-view-wrap-lines nil)`, `q`, `M-o v`: lines are cut off as before\n- [ ] Regression: the sidebar (`C-x t s`) and an Org buffer are unchanged (no new wrapping)\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Close the view: `M-o v` (or `q` in it).\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .`.\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`; restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`).\n- Optionally delete the test branch: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 456-vulpea-ui-view-wrap-lines`.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCe4rx9pfC1dArkw75)_",
